BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 7 Tf 48 30 Td (The Inspection Playbook · free from Staffbook · staffbook.co.uk) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 7 Tf 525.1 30 Td (Page 3) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 771.89 Td (6. Staffing rotas) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 753.89 Td (The rota as planned, and evidence of what actually happened when reality diverged.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 735.89 Td (Good looks like: published rotas, corrected when swaps happen, with cover levels and a first aider on every shift.) Tj ET
BT 0.7 0.15 0.15 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 58 717.89 Td (What fails:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 704.39 Td (a rota that says one thing while everyone knows the month went differently.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 686.39 Td (Fix this week: check last month's rota against what really happened. Correct it. That correction is the record.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 658.39 Td (7. Allegations records) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 640.39 Td (Held securely, with the timescales evidenced: reported to a senior manager immediately, the designated officer told) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 627.39 Td (within one working day.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 609.39 Td (Good looks like: a locked record showing dates for every step, however uncomfortable the content.) Tj ET
BT 0.7 0.15 0.15 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 58 591.39 Td (What fails:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 577.89 Td (an allegation everyone remembers but nobody wrote down at the time.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 559.89 Td (Fix this week: check the last allegation record shows its dates. If there has never been one, check the team knows) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 546.89 Td (the reporting steps cold.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 518.89 Td (8. Regulation 44 reports) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 500.89 Td (The independent visitor, every month, and what happened to the actions they raised.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 482.89 Td (Good looks like: a full run of months, each report filed, each action closed and traceable.) Tj ET
BT 0.7 0.15 0.15 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 58 464.89 Td (What fails:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 451.39 Td (a missing month. Actions raised in March still open in August with no note why.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 433.39 Td (Fix this week: fill the visit grid on the Governance clocks tab. A missed month is a breach; know before they do.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 405.39 Td (9. Regulation 45 review) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 387.39 Td (Your own six-month review of the quality of care, sent to Ofsted within 28 days of completion.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 369.39 Td (Good looks like: built from the home's own records, honest about weaknesses, with actions that then actually) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 356.39 Td (happened.) Tj ET
BT 0.7 0.15 0.15 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 58 338.39 Td (What fails:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 324.89 Td (overdue, or glowing in a way your own records contradict.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 306.89 Td (Fix this week: find the date of your last one. Add six months. Put the deadline in the diary.) Tj ET
BT 0.05 0.36 0.27 rg /F2 11 Tf 48 278.89 Td (10. Notifications) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 48 260.89 Td (The serious events you told Ofsted about, within 24 hours, with who else was told and what was done.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 242.89 Td (Good looks like: a log that matches reality: every notifiable event, notified, with the follow-up recorded.) Tj ET
BT 0.7 0.15 0.15 rg /F2 9.5 Tf 58 224.89 Td (What fails:) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 211.39 Td (an event in the daily logs that never became a notification.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 193.39 Td (Fix this week: agree with your team, in one sentence each, what counts as notifiable. Ambiguity is where these get) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 9.5 Tf 58 180.39 Td (missed.) Tj ET
endstream
