BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 7 Tf 48 30 Td (The Inspection Playbook · free from Staffbook · staffbook.co.uk) Tj ET
BT 0.42 0.45 0.44 rg /F1 7 Tf 525.1 30 Td (Page 5) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 15 Tf 48 763.89 Td (Script one: the employment gap conversation) Tj ET
0.75 0.8 0.78 RG 0.6 w 48 757.89 m 547.28 757.89 l S
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 735.89 Td (You have found a hole in someone's work history. Here is the whole conversation. It takes two minutes and it is) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 721.39 Td (not an accusation.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 701.89 Td ("While I was tidying the files I noticed a gap in your work history, between [month] and [month]. It is) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 687.39 Td (completely normal, I just need one line in writing about what that period was. Travelling, family, between) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 672.89 Td (jobs, anything. What was it?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 653.39 Td (Then write exactly what they say, date it, and put it in the file. Done. If they cannot remember precisely, "believed) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 638.89 Td (to be between roles" dated today is still a written explanation.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 619.39 Td (The rule: written down is a pass, silence is a finding. Never leave the conversation without the sentence.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 15 Tf 48 585.89 Td (Script two: the reference verification call) Tj ET
0.75 0.8 0.78 RG 0.6 w 48 579.89 m 547.28 579.89 l S
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 557.89 Td (A written reference is a claim. This call makes it evidence. Ring the organisation's main number, not the mobile) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 543.39 Td (on the letter, and ask for the person who signed it.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 523.89 Td ("Hello, I'm [name], manager at a children's home. [Person] has applied to work with us and gave us a) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 509.39 Td (reference in your name. Can I take two minutes to confirm it? Did you write it? Can you confirm the dates) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 494.89 Td (they worked with you, and their role? Why did they leave? And the one I have to ask: would you employ) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 480.39 Td (them again, in work around children?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 460.89 Td (Then two lines on paper: who you spoke to, when, and what they confirmed. Date it, initial it, staple it to the) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 446.39 Td (reference. That note is what inspectors look for.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 426.89 Td (If the referee hesitates on the last question, that hesitation is the most useful thing the call could have) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 412.39 Td (given you. Follow it.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
